{"content":[{"c":["MADMEN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town in Moab, according to Jeremiah’s oracle (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.48.2","r":"Jer.48.2","rawR":"Jer.48.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.48.2","value":"Jer.48.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 48:2"},"). It may be a form created by dittography from an original Dimon, as in the oracle against Moab by Isaiah (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.15.9","r":"Isa.15.9","rawR":"Isa.15.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.15.9","value":"Isa.15.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 15:9"},"). If so, Khirbet Dimneh, seven and a half miles (12.1 kilometers) northwest of Kerak at the head of Wadi Beni Hammad, would be a possible site. In any case, there is a word play in the Jeremiah passage between the place-name and the Hebrew word “be silent.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Madmen","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 48:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.48.2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.48.2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.48.2"},{"anchorText":"Is 15:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.15.9","rawQueryValue":"Isa.15.9","sourceRefExact":"Isa.15.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"95f19e33a5cb80efd16fd876279c74612a0644ce914c576ebc35090c224e9471","sourceItemName":"Madmen","sourceItemOrder":37,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Madmen","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Madmen","title":"Madmen","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}